#X obj 604 638 float 1, f 9;
#X text 896 578 >7) Float takes the number is is given by its creation argument and outputs it upon a [bang]. If there is a number given to its cold inlet it outputs that upon the [bang].;
#X text 890 651 >8) So the count and reset to the left sends out a signal at 0 but then adds 1 to it. That feeds into the [mod 10] which produces a number to the [trigger float float]. The [trigger float float] first sends that number back up to the [float] which stores that number. Then the [trigger float float] sends the same number to the number atom below. Upon the next [bang] the stored number in [float] has 1 added to it and the goes on and on. However \, because [mod 10] produces a 0 when the number it is fed reaches 10 \, it then sends out a 0 to reset the count.;
